  "from": "postrank-explorer-v1 verification/readouts/two-units.json",
  "about": "Two independent normal posteriors. The read-out gives pi_AB, pi_BA, the posterior mean and SD of the difference A minus B and the size of the gap in SDs of the difference (with above, below or apart in words); the worked formula repeats them with the four settings; the reverse line gives pi_BA = 1 - pi_AB; the sliders show the settings. Ported from v1's core cases: the Deeper boxes' cases moved with their content to apps 1.9 and 1.10, the two scripted predictions were dropped (v3 has no prediction gate), the corr and mixW slider outputs left gap20, and the caption reads in its v3 wording. Probabilities are rows of the base-R oracle (oracle-pairwise, pairDirection); the gap, the SD of the difference and the gap in SDs come from v1's frozen registry (cf.pair.*, settings.*). The clamped case moves both means past the slider ends: pi_BA equals the oracle value at means 2 and -2 only if both were clamped there. New in v3: the preset for tutorial sites A and B, the read-out sentences word for word (slotted literals), the reverse line's condition, the upper table, legends and slider names, and means 2 and -2 with SDs .05, where the doubles of both probabilities are exactly 1 and 0 and read as bounds (CR-008), as pi_AB does in the clamped case. Review 044 repair (X-01): the area labels of the difference figure carry pi_AB and pi_BA (\"pi_AB = .760 ->\", a bound as a relation); cases gap20, wide-b, clamped-far and far-narrow check both against the same oracle rows as the read-out.",
